editorial_contributions.text:
In this work, the author establishes simple inequalities for the integrals

\[ \int_0^x \mathrm{e}^{-\gamma t} rac{I_{
u}(t)}{t^{
u}}\,\mathrm{d}t, \quad \int_x^{\infty} \mathrm{e}^{\gamma t} rac{K_{
u}(t)}{t^{
u}}\,\mathrm{d}t, \quad x>0,\,\,\,0\le \gamma<1, 	ag{1} \]

involving modified Bessel functions of the first kind \(I_{
u}(x)\) and the second kind \(K_{
u}(x)\). Integrals of the form (1) for specific values of \(\gamma\) are tabulated in standard references, like, e.g. in [	extit{F. W. J. Olver} and 	extit{L. C. Maximon}, ``Bessel functions'', in: NIST handbook of mathematical functions. U.S. Dept. Commerce, Washington, DC. 215--286 (2010)]. For \(\gamma=0\), the integrals in (1) can be represented by means of the generalized hypergeometric function. However, for \(\gamma
e0\), related general closed-form representations do not seem to have appeared in the existing literature.

The developed methodology for deriving bounds for the integrals in (1) consists in exploiting basic identities and monotonicity properties of the modified Bessel functions; these properties are included in the Appendix B. The main results of the paper are given in Theorems 2.1 and 2.6 and are based on an inequality involving the modified Bessel function \(K_{
u}(x)\), which is proved in the Appendix A. The conditions on \(
u\) are different for several of the derived inequalities. In most considered cases, the inequalities are tight in certain limits. Furthermore, a tight double inequality for a generalized hypergeometric function, involving \(I_{
u}(x)\), is obtained as a corollary. Finally, an open problem for the above integral for \(I_{
u}(x)\) is also posed.
